fuxi: 0103 -- multithreaded UFS root device (8 slots, one per core)

Rebased from fuxi-ufs-fast 0101, which was a full-file replacement written
against the pre-rename UFS driver.  The content here is that patch's output with
the rename's token map applied to identifiers, the log prefixes, the log magic
and the driver externs, so it lands on the post-rename file rather than next to
it.  Two deliberate nits on top of the mechanical rename: the file header says
FUXI, and the tsleep channel label is "fuxilog" -- a wait-channel label, not the
fuxilog= boot argument, which is untouched.

The root driver issued polled SCSI commands ONE at a time behind a single global
mutex, with a single UTRD, a single UCD and a single 1 MiB bounce buffer.  Even
with cpus=8 every filesystem read queued behind that lock, which is why a cold
boot takes minutes: the dyld shared cache alone is 3.3 GB read in 4 KiB blocks,
~800k commands serialised end to end.

The host exposes 32 UTRL slots (CAP low 5 bits = 0x1F); Linux's ufshcd would run
can_queue = 31.  This takes 8 -- one per core -- which captures the available
parallelism for HFS+/dyld workloads without the tag-map machinery of a 31-deep
queue:

  * each slot owns its own UTRD, UCD (128-byte aligned) and 1 MiB bounce buffer
  * one contiguous DMA allocation; the host is not cache coherent, so each slot
    cleans/invalidates only its own ranges
  * only the slot's own doorbell bit is rung, and only that bit is polled
  * the global lock now covers only slot allocation and rare state changes
  * REG_IS is cleared only when the whole doorbell is idle

DMA layout verified to fit: 8 UTRDs end at 0x100, 8 UCDs at 0x3400, bounce area
starts at 0x4000, 8.02 MiB total.

Write fence, unchanged from the original patch and from the pre-0103 file:
- GPT fence is 'lba + count - 1 >= gpt_alt', not the 'gpt_alt - 4' that the
  proposed code had.  With the backup GPT at 61850619 that variant began at
  61850615, but userdata runs to 61850618 and the persistent log ring occupies
  its final 4 MiB, so every log flush would have been refused and the log
  thread would have stopped silently.  The margin is unnecessary because
  ufs_write_blocks_slot already rejects anything outside the partition bounds
  before this check.
- partition bounds, 'lba < 6' and the <= UINT32_MAX guard are byte-for-byte
  what 0028/0030 established.

THIS PATCH IS A FULL-FILE REPLACEMENT relative to the post-0102 file: its hunks
are generated against 0102-applied content, so it must be applied AFTER 0102.
Guards against the failure mode that hid an earlier attempt: the build treats an
unappliable patch as a warning and carries on, so 'CI success' alone does not
prove this applied -- check the kernel strings for 'slots (MT)' and
'FUXI UFS: command' as the real gate, and check the CI log for
'Skipping patch ... 0103'.

Deferred: interrupts.  Still polled (REG_IE=0) and each slot polls only its own
doorbell bit, so latencies now overlap instead of stacking, but completion is
still detected by polling.  REG_IE plus a completion path is the next step.
